  "name": "Futerkon",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Futerkon is a series of furry conventions in Poland, held annually in August and aimed mainly at the Polish-speaking furry community. It is the Polish national furry convention and a direct continuation of Futrzakon, with new staff and new concepts. First held August 8 to 11, 2012, it puts integration first: a large bonfire meet and greet with a dance opens each convention, the yearly theme drives the scheduled events, and an open-field game tells a story that unfolds in an after-dark exploration game. A recent addition is a meeting with a guest of honor from outside the furry world. It is run by an independent group.",
